    "message": "Judge: alex's old-schema corridors oriented by geometry; S7 judges alex routes on them\n\nThe toolkit's loader did not have judgex.py's reversal bug: it never read the corridor\nedges, so alex's bent holes were simply unjudged by S7 (and drawn as tee->basket chords).\n- ports/judge/testimony.mjs corridorOf: each edge oriented tee -> basket by geometry (alex\n  stores #1's right edge basket -> tee, #2/#3's tee -> basket), paired; centreline + widths.\n  Real annotation: widths 32.5-37.6 (hole 16), 28.6-35.0 (13), 28.7-34.4 (6) px.\n- holePaths carries the centreline and median width; judgeHoleTraces judges an old-schema\n  route on it (end within 12 px, within W / 2); bends stay unjudged (bendsJudged: false).\n- compare.mjs draws that centreline instead of the chord; s7trace run.mjs --attempts-root.\n- alex (attempt-1792426160776-46e5ad0c22a0), routeMatch: 3/3 agree (holes 6, 13, 16 off the\n  centreline 3.5, 8.4, 1.4 px; W / 2 = 16.8 px).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EiRF33JBG7FEiMhXczeLaq",
